  'An iconic tropical climbing hemiepiphyte renowned for its enormous, glossy, perforated and deeply split emerald-green leaves and stout aerial cord roots.',
  ARRAY['Massive climbing vine with stout stems producing thick, cord-like brownish aerial roots', 'Huge, glossy, heart-shaped leathery leaves that develop dramatic natural perforations (fenestrations) and deep splits', 'Creamy-white boat-shaped spathe enclosing a stout spadix that develops into an edible cob-like fruit', 'Fruit covered in hexagonal green scales that pop off naturally when fully ripe to reveal sweet pineapple-banana pulp']::text[],
  'Tropical rainforest understory, climbing up mature host trees, and stylish interior spaces.',
