  'The State Flower of Assam and Arunachal Pradesh, a magnificent monopodial epiphyte with thick leathery leaves and long pendulous, cylindrical flower clusters resembling a fluffy fox tail.',
  ARRAY['Monopodial epiphytic growth habit with stout, climbing stems and thick, spongy silvery-white velamen-covered aerial roots', 'Curved, channelled, leathery strap-like leaves with uneven, praemorse (bitten-off) tips', 'Spectacular pendulous cylindrical racemes (up to 30-40 cm long) densely packed with over 100 miniature spotted flowers', 'Flowers are white to pale pink, heavily spotted and flushed with vibrant magenta-purple, emitting a sweet spicy fragrance']::text[],
