  'An aggressive, noxious invasive annual weed with carrot-like dissected leaves, angular grooved stems, and small creamy-white flower heads. SEVERE HUMAN ALLERGEN AND LIVESTOCK TOXIN.',
  ARRAY['Erect, vigorously branching annual herb up to 1 to 2 meters tall with deeply grooved, longitudinally striated hairy stems', 'Deeply dissected, pale green, alternate leaves resembling carrot foliage (hence ''Carrot Grass'')', 'Hundreds of miniature, star-shaped creamy-white flower heads (capitula) clustered in loose terminal panicles', 'Prolific seed producer: a single mature plant can produce up to 25,000 viable seeds']::text[],
